{"_id":"U0cRZvrvdyQCKHy8","name":"Action Procedure","pages":[{"_id":"wM8rKr23BuagUvrK","name":"Action Procedure","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eWhen the players take action the Referee works down this list:\u003c/p\u003e\u003col\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIntent: What are you trying to do?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eLeverage: What makes it possible?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eCost: Would it use a resource, cause Virtue Loss, or have a side-effect?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eRisk: What\u0027s at risk? No risk, no roll. Otherwise make a Save or a Luck Roll.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eImpact: Show the consequences, honour the established risk, and move forward.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003ch3\u003eSUCCESS\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen the players succeed at a significant action the Referee does one of the following:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAdvance: Move in a good direction.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDisrupt: Lessen a threat.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eResolve: Put a problem to rest.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch3\u003eFAILURE\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen the players fail at a risky action they might still complete the action, but always suffer negative consequences:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThreaten: Create a new problem.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEscalate: Make a problem worse.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eExecute: Deliver on a threat.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch3\u003eIMPACT\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhether a success or a failure, ensure that the players’ actions have an observable impact on the world. The best types of impact have both immediate and lasting consequences, always moving things forward.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 16\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"dTFXxMAWosNhSU3i","name":"Advancing Time","pages":[{"_id":"RTRTod1HRFUljgia","name":"Advancing Time","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eAt the end of each session, or during a natural break in their journey, the group decides how much time will reasonably pass:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNone\u003c/strong\u003e: Pick up where you left off.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWeeks\u003c/strong\u003e: Continue on to the next significant seasonal event.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMonths\u003c/strong\u003e: Move to the next Season.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYears\u003c/strong\u003e: Begin a new Age in Spring.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf uncertain, roll:\u003c/p\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e[[/r 1d6]]\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ch3\u003ePASSAGE OF TIME\u003c/h3\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e1\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.BuleIJa3bFxPopzQ]{Season} or @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.9btBt0rE5AvXw3mt]{Age} turns \u003cstrong\u003enow.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e2-3\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.BuleIJa3bFxPopzQ]{Season} or @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.9btBt0rE5AvXw3mt]{Age} turns \u003cstrong\u003eafter next session.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e4-6\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.BuleIJa3bFxPopzQ]{Season} or @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.9btBt0rE5AvXw3mt]{Age} \u003cstrong\u003econtinues.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eBETWEEN SEASONS\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eRestore @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.a3wuqgFMQEMjrm0S]{Virtues}and choose one:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePilgrimage\u003c/strong\u003e: Learn about an unknown part of the Realm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCourtesy\u003c/strong\u003e: Establish a new contact or earn a favour.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eService\u003c/strong\u003e: Make a small improvement to the Realm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eBETWEEN AGES\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eRestore @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.a3wuqgFMQEMjrm0S]{Virtues}, gain 1 @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.p1BbrqwB3IL5KnsP]{Glory}, choose one:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDuty\u003c/strong\u003e: Make a significant improvement to the Realm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSuccession\u003c/strong\u003e: Establish a successor and/or have them Knighted.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLegacy\u003c/strong\u003e: Your successor gains half of your current Glory.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 17\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"9btBt0rE5AvXw3mt","name":"Ages","pages":[{"_id":"76z6ct8IPxvTmAMA","name":"Ages","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eEach \u003cstrong\u003eLife\u003c/strong\u003e has 3 \u003cstrong\u003eAges\u003c/strong\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYoung:\u003c/strong\u003e Green, always learning.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMature:\u003c/strong\u003e Seasoned, in their golden years.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOld:\u003c/strong\u003e Grey, considering their legacy.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen a character becomes \u003cstrong\u003eMature\u003c/strong\u003e they reroll each Virtue on [[/r d12+d6]] and keep the result if higher.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen a character becomes \u003cstrong\u003eOld\u003c/strong\u003e they reroll each Virtue on [[/r d12+d6]] and keep the result if lower. Old characters lose [[/r d12]] \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003e at the end of each Age. If this takes them to VIG 0 they die peacefully.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 10\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"BmeUt7Yesk8hRT73","name":"Attacks","pages":[{"_id":"2SQ8etAJFLKJHK1l","name":"Attacks","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eTake the Attack dice noted on your weapon(s), shield, and granted by bonuses.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eGo through the following steps in order:\u003c/p\u003e\u003col\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAll combatants attacking the same target roll their dice at the same time.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf the target or their nearby allies can @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.G4QYjtCVWeZP6YIA]{Deny}they may use it.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAttackers may perform @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.U8Vl83tcDkRYLmpZ]{Gambits}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eTake the highest die remaining.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAdd any extra Damage from attackers who are @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.U8Vl83tcDkRYLmpZ]{Bolstering} the Attack.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSubtract the target’s total Armour score.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Attack causes that much Damage.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003cp\u003eSo a Knight with a mace (d8) and shield (d4) is aided by an ally with 2 daggers (d6 each). They roll d8 and d4, and 2d6 respectively. The dice show 7, 3, 1, and 5. The highest die is 7. The 5 is spent on a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.U8Vl83tcDkRYLmpZ]{Gambit} to Bolster the Damage to 8. The target has Armour 2 (helm and shield), reducing the Damage to 6.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eImpaired\u003c/strong\u003e attacks roll d4 only and cannot gain bonus dice or benefit from Feats.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBlast\u003c/strong\u003e attacks target everybody in their area, rolling each separately.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 8\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"CapdrFIR5fQTiMqQ","name":"Barriers","pages":[{"_id":"mOXxasc4HwI7Kxrt","name":"Barriers","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eTravel through a Barrier is not normally possible, though locals might know a way. Attempting to travel through a Barrier wastes that Phase of the day, but still causes a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.PxSDkx5wU6kRX5V3]{Wilderness Roll}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 8\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"wth6UnvG7N5dmqeQ","name":"Between Ages","pages":[{"_id":"066ro5Z0GEuhbZNS","name":"Between Ages","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eRestore @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.a3wuqgFMQEMjrm0S]{Virtues}, gain 1 @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.p1BbrqwB3IL5KnsP]{Glory}, choose one:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDuty\u003c/strong\u003e: Make a significant improvement to the Realm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSuccession\u003c/strong\u003e: Establish a successor and/or have them Knighted.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLegacy\u003c/strong\u003e: Your successor gains half of your current Glory.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 17\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"KrrH14Q3jHr5CGMt","name":"Between Seasons","pages":[{"_id":"tzsSVfLF5QesIpPh","name":"Between Seasons","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eRestore Virtues and choose one:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePilgrimage\u003c/strong\u003e: Learn about an unknown part of the Realm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCourtesy\u003c/strong\u003e: Establish a new contact or earn a favour.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eService\u003c/strong\u003e: Make a small improvement to the Realm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 17\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"Q84GshhKtznJytyY","name":"Blast","pages":[{"_id":"8P3Hmkg7X0NMdpMs","name":"Blast","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBlast\u003c/strong\u003e attacks target everybody in their area, rolling each separately.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 8\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"P2f6vJkFqnxeT07b","name":"Bonus Attack Dice","pages":[{"_id":"tS7z1vtKPTgWyaQd","name":"Bonus Attack Dice","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eThese are gained from useful information, shrewd preparations, or a tactical advantage. +[[/r d8]] is a typical bonus.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"sVtJ8E9xvI1n5yAY","name":"Camping","pages":[{"_id":"4GXtviV0v71dYtn3","name":"Camping","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eWhen sleeping outdoors make a  @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.PxSDkx5wU6kRX5V3]{Wilderness Roll} as normal, ignoring Landmarks. Hostile Omens prevent proper sleep, while others may not occur at all if they are improbable as nighttime activity.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 18\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"XM3smSOyDUeVgMWz","name":"Claiming a Seat of Power","pages":[{"_id":"pTrSLAIi50gcs9aL","name":"Claiming a Seat of Power","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eA @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.ml5gCjU1JAnzXajw]{Seat of Power} carries similar problems to a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.dJeZTvmudZnjrS96]{Holding}, elevated to a larger scale. Threats arise from within your @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.X1lghTTFxdKGH1z4]{Court}, within your @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.3hsMdqsglAWNjUQu]{Realm}, and from @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.ehLtyf20u7JwlsrK]{beyond your borders}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 20\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"huwiNNXfDFVEkVan","name":"Conquest","pages":[{"_id":"sQo4n4eljvDYKbmB","name":"Conquest","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eKnights live between two worlds. One of rank, oath, and rule of the worthy. The other of chaos, brutality, and rule of the strong.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOften, having the audacity to seat yourself in a Holding is enough to make you the ruler.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eHoldings and Realms seized by force and left unchallenged tend to have a period of turmoil before adapting to the new status quo.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 21\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"jao8p4SpbPMN1KyH","name":"Courtly Conflict","pages":[{"_id":"QX6xe8u1A4HbLPxD","name":"Courtly Conflict","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eCourtiers breed problems, especially when they hold leverage over their ruler, whether family influence, dark secrets, or military might. Here a ruler must tread carefully, as obvious solutions always leave at least one party feeling mistreated.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEvery Season brings some drama. Spark Tables can help to describe this.\u003cbr /\u003eRoll to see how you’re involved:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"376\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e[[/r d6]]\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ch3\u003eDRAMA IN COURT\u003c/h3\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"376\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e1\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are \u003cstrong\u003epersonally involved\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"376\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e2-3\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are involved \u003cstrong\u003eby association\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"376\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e4-6\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are \u003cstrong\u003enot involved\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 21\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"47edfac2-5fe9-4679-8b0b-dcbf300b7c29","name":"Creating a Realm","pages":[{"_id":"mZwJSHizggUf6lDo","name":"Creating a Realm","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003ch3\u003eBREAKING THE RULES\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe guidelines on this page make for a typical Realm, but they can be bent or broken in creating your own Realms.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eTHE HEX MAP\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eA Realm is mapped on a hexagonal grid covering the loose rule of a Seat of Power. A 12x12 grid is typical, whether the Realm is landlocked, coastal, or an island chain.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTypically, players get a copy of the map with Holdings and general terrain marked. They cannot see Myths, Landmarks, and Barriers.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe distance covered by each hexagon is a \u003cstrong\u003eHecksleague\u003c/strong\u003e, commonly called a Hex.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis distance represents a few loose factors:\u003c/p\u003e\u003col\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003c/span\u003eThe area a hill fort can overlook\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003c/span\u003eThe area that guards can patrol in a day\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003c/span\u003eA return hike to a neighbouring Hex gets you home before dark\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003ch3\u003eWILDERNESS\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eMost Hexes are Wilderness, with a variety of terrain types. \u003ca\u003eSpark Tables\u003c/a\u003e can help with this. As a general guide create clusters of [[/r d12]] hexes of the same terrain type.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSome Hexes have a Barrier on one or more of their edges, typically a sudden altitude change or impassible feature. These cannot normally be travelled through. For a typical Realm, place a number of Barriers equal to one sixth of your total Hexes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMost Realms have a navigable river passing through and a few large lakes spanning whole or multiple Hexes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eHOLDINGS\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003ePlace 4 Holdings a good distance apart, typically castles, walled towns, fortresses, or towers, held by Knights or influential Vassals. Most of the Realm lives within their walls or the surrounding Hex.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDesignate one Holding as the Seat of Power. This is the Holding of the ruler of the whole Realm, commonly a Knight.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eMYTH HEXES\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003ePlace 6 \u003ca href=\"/browse/myths\"\u003eMyths\u003c/a\u003e in remote places. Number them as 1-6. The Hexes are clearly affected by the presence of their Myth.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eLANDMARKS\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eSome Wilderness Hexes contain a Landmark. These are discovered when travellers roll 4-6 on the Wilderness roll. A typical Realm has 3 or 4 of each type of Landmark. Mark them with their initial or an icon.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEven characters who know a Landmark’s location must still make a Wilderness Roll to check for Omens as they travel there.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEach Landmark type covers a range of specific features, with prompts provided on Knight and Myth pages later in the book.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe course of the game may create new Landmarks or remove or alter existing ones.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe 6 types of landmarks are:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003c/span\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.gEhHqMT5ciuQNZXm]{Dwellings}\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003c/span\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.QWZ5Xsa3vuo5Bf69]{Sanctums}\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003c/span\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.lBdvsLmaxCzXExnv]{Monuments}\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003c/span\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.UuZ3UFDChYMN7gTh]{Hazards}\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003c/span\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.ihrxnfnNnK4x8KPd]{Curses}\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003c/span\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.TuBkbx1jAFCmrp19]{Ruins}\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch3\u003eADDING DETAILS\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca\u003eSpark Tables\u003c/a\u003e can add detail to significant locations and people in the Realm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eDISTANT REALMS\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eRealms are usually bordered by water, mountains, or wasteland, though claims are often disputed. Travelling to a distant Realm normally sees you arrive in the next Season.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 14\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"VKF3X9roMxCO2nPp","name":"Crises","pages":[{"_id":"S9QccXQbrkUkz1RJ","name":"Crises","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Ht6YdS1x8Va8s16q]{Ruling a Domain} is an exercise in ongoing disaster management.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt the start of a Season or when returning from a long absence, roll:\u003c/p\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e[[/r d6]]\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ch3\u003eCRISIS ROLL\u003c/h3\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e1\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCalamity\u003c/strong\u003e: Immediately gain 2 Crises.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e2-3\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDilemma\u003c/strong\u003e: Choose between 2 Crises.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e4-6\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProsperity\u003c/strong\u003e: Times are good.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003cp\u003eCrises apply to the whole Domain, not a single character, and remain until resolved.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThey can be chosen by the Referee, or rolled:\u003c/p\u003e\u003col\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eChaos\u003c/strong\u003e - Lawlessness in the land Resolution: Enforce a sense of justice.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDebt\u003c/strong\u003e - Dire need of coffer and coin Resolution: Restock the treasury.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFamine\u003c/strong\u003e - Empty plates, empty fields Resolution: Get food into the stores.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMisery\u003c/strong\u003e - Vassals question why they toil Resolution: Raise the spirits of the people.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePanic\u003c/strong\u003e - The weak tremble with unease Resolution: Ensure the Vassals feel safe.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDoubt\u003c/strong\u003e - Seeds of betrayal against you Resolution: Assert your authority to rule.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf a season ends with 3 or more unresolved Crises then the Domain goes into @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.T74kT3xY6yPC3MK2]{Misrule}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 20\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ihrxnfnNnK4x8KPd","name":"Curses","pages":[{"_id":"BjA3JG0luYjCIbA0","name":"Curses","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eBlights on the land that throw you off course. If you travel in the next Phase it counts as @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.730Af1FmIdloG4vY]{Travelling Blind}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 14\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"Uk3I1q1ontYnrY2A","name":"Damage","pages":[{"_id":"KGVcnOBXkagCf667","name":"Damage","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eThe attack’s Damage is deducted from the target’s \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eGD\u003c/span\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf they have at least 1GD remaining then they Evade the Attack.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf it leaves them with exactly 0GD then they gain a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.sc76aTlM7OLBPigZ]{Scar}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf it exceeds the target’s GD, the excess is deducted from \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003e and they are Wounded.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf they lose half or more of their remaining VIG it is a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Kkozior5c3JbSn39]{Mortal Wound}. Mortally Wounded targets are down and dying. They die if left untended for an hour, but can be patched up\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ein a few moments.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf Damage reduces the target’s VIG to 0, they are @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.277DeX9r1AioelSw]{Slain}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 8\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"277DeX9r1AioelSw","name":"Death","pages":[{"_id":"WBym2YPZf1V4Bsoz","name":"Death","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eEven the boldest Knight can die a sudden or ignoble death. Prepare yourself for this.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen a Knight dies the player creates a new Knight and they are added to the Company as quickly as possible. Alternatively they may assume control of a Squire or follower.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 8\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"G4QYjtCVWeZP6YIA","name":"Deny","pages":[{"_id":"HIKKIuNA58zVtSfe","name":"Deny","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eRebuff an attack before it lands\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUse after an Attack roll against you or an ally within arm’s reach.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDiscard one Attack die from the roll.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePass a \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eSPI\u003c/span\u003e Save or become Fatigued.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"1awKBfGuG7xMbNIx","name":"Dire Weather","pages":[{"_id":"qESv3OwrZyhcL5Oh","name":"Dire Weather","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eWhen travelling in lands at the mercy of dire weather, roll at the start of each Phase.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"64\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e[[/r 1d6]]\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ch3\u003eDIRE WEATHER\u003c/h3\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"64\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e1\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDire weather. \u003c/strong\u003eYou can’t leave the Hex and can’t get proper sleep.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"64\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e2-3\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLooming threat\u003c/strong\u003e. If this is rolled a second consecutive time, treat as dire weather.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"64\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e4-6\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFine weather\u003c/strong\u003e for travel.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 18\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ehLtyf20u7JwlsrK","name":"Distant Realms","pages":[{"_id":"jqlarxqGk46jxixJ","name":"Distant Realms","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.3hsMdqsglAWNjUQu]{Realms} are usually bordered by water, mountains, or wasteland, though claims are often disputed. Travelling to a distant Realm normally sees you arrive in the next Season.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 14\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"M7caQ5muj7rvEfh3","name":"Duels \u0026 Jousts","pages":[{"_id":"ufenJRS7HbLKRovi","name":"Duels \u0026 Jousts","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eTwo combatants can mutually agree to engage in a duel, or joust if mounted.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThey fight as normal but their attacks are rolled and resolved simultaneously, including the effects of Gambits. Both combatants can use Feats before the attacks are resolved.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"gEhHqMT5ciuQNZXm","name":"Dwellings","pages":[{"_id":"SdyUMT96K7EU9k4m","name":"Dwellings","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eSets of humble homes amidst the wilds.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 14\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"Lq3J9OOZ8F1DhFXq","name":"Ending A Session","pages":[{"_id":"y5KpJFsjKNyTxHHE","name":"Ending A Session","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eAt the end of each session:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDiscuss if it would feel right for a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.BuleIJa3bFxPopzQ]{Season} or @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.9btBt0rE5AvXw3mt]{Age} to pass between now and the next session.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf a Season or Age passes, then follow the procedure detailed.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAsk the players if they have any plans or ambitions for the next session. This gives you a direction for any preparation you do before then.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 16\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"KVv0zNVXVsh9Qquy","name":"Exploration Actions","pages":[{"_id":"I0HXeaz8BFVpHRtn","name":"Exploration Actions","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eWhen ruling exploration actions, follow the standard @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.U0cRZvrvdyQCKHy8]{Action Procedure}. In particular, consider whether the action will take a whole Phase of the day to carry out.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs with other Actions, the players should know the risks before they commit to it.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf the Action calls for a Save the Company decides who rolls, using their Virtue.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEven if they fail the Save, the goal might still be achievable, but now faces an obstacle, a hostile encounter, or an additional cost.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhile the cause and consequence of failure can be personal, they also represent the whims of nature, bad weather, shifting land.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf it is unclear which Virtue to use, consider the main activity involved in the risky part:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVigour\u003c/strong\u003e: Strength or physical stamina.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eClarity\u003c/strong\u003e: Senses or mental quickness.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSpirit\u003c/strong\u003e: Social or emotional influence.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 19\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"h9e6V7nLciONrfTO","name":"Exposed","pages":[{"_id":"uzHzw6x3cr1DPYIR","name":"Exposed","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eCharacters who are caught with their guard down or otherwise defenceless are \u003cem\u003eExposed\u003c/em\u003e and act as if they have 0\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eGD\u003c/span\u003e. If they remedy their situation then they are no longer \u003cem\u003eExposed\u003c/em\u003e. Traps and ambushes typically catch victims \u003cem\u003eExposed\u003c/em\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 8\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"WgapBijp9UUG9CWT","name":"Faith","pages":[{"_id":"sRxhCGmAwA7a8FUr","name":"Faith","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSome believe there is truth in the sky: the stars, moon, sun, positions, and motions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSome look to nature: the turn of seasons, the sound of trees, the wisdom of beasts.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSome believe the sacred stories that weave into Myths, guiding us to the City.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 13\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"h4ATNWH8WwUmQNdC","name":"Fatigue","pages":[{"_id":"J5fxlhhqRyHQK5Re","name":"Fatigue","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eA \u003cem\u003eFatigued\u003c/em\u003e character is unable to use \u003cstrong\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Ii4ZqGwzc3qZWA8B]{Feats}\u003c/strong\u003e until they rest.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 10\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"Ii4ZqGwzc3qZWA8B","name":"Feats","pages":[{"_id":"UJZVjOUkvNL5lnmA","name":"Feats","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eThese special actions known by Knights can be performed as described. Using Feats risks the Knight becoming Fatigued which prevents them from using further Feats until they rest.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAfter using a Feat the user must pass a Save or become \u003cem\u003eFatigued\u003c/em\u003e, unable to perform Feats until they rest. Each Feat can only be used once per Attack by each combatant involved.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSMITE\u003c/strong\u003e - \u003cem\u003eRelease your righteous fury\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUse before rolling a melee Attack.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Attack gains either +[[/r d12]]or @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Q84GshhKtznJytyY]{Blast}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePass a \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003e Save or become Fatigued.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFOCUS\u003c/strong\u003e - \u003cem\u003eCreate an opening to exploit\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUse after rolling an Attack.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePerform a Gambit without using a die.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePass a \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eCLA\u003c/span\u003e Save or become Fatigued.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDENY \u003c/strong\u003e- \u003cem\u003eRebuff an attack before it lands\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUse after an Attack roll against you or an ally within arm’s reach.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDiscard one Attack die from the roll.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePass a \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eSPI\u003c/span\u003e Save or become Fatigued.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"OVaEls1kihdxQT3g","name":"Focus","pages":[{"_id":"7bzslOTExYRsXV3q","name":"Focus","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCreate an opening to exploit\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUse after rolling an Attack.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePerform a Gambit without using a die.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePass a \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eCLA\u003c/span\u003e Save or become Fatigued\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"U8Vl83tcDkRYLmpZ","name":"Gambits","pages":[{"_id":"04T6Yf6IZkViQs8i","name":"Gambits","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eAttackers may discard any number of Attack dice of 4 or higher to perform Gambits, each causing one of the effects below. The affected foe must be a target of the original attack.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor Gambits other than \u003cem\u003eBolster\u003c/em\u003e and \u003cem\u003eMove\u003c/em\u003e the target receives a \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003e Save to ignore the effect.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBolster\u003c/strong\u003e the Attack for +1 total Damage\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMove\u003c/strong\u003e after the Attack, even if you already moved or are unable to move\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRepel\u003c/strong\u003e a foe away from you\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStop\u003c/strong\u003e a foe from moving next turn\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.w0AdMBWGQLWhQHd8]{Impair} \u003c/strong\u003ea weapon on their next turn\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTrap\u003c/strong\u003e a shield until your next turn\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.arw6LSD4H5hvFDS3]{Dismount} \u003c/strong\u003ea foe\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOther\u003c/strong\u003e \u003cstrong\u003eeffect\u003c/strong\u003e of a similar level of impact\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf a die of 8 or higher is used in melee then a \u003cstrong\u003eStrong Gambit\u003c/strong\u003e is performed and the attacker chooses one of the following:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNo Save\u003c/strong\u003e is granted to the target\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGreater effect\u003c/strong\u003e such as disarming an item, breaking a wooden shield or weapon, or removing a helm. This does not increase the Damage from Bolster.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"i8dUaR1tAtVnnkTd","name":"Gathering Folklore","pages":[{"_id":"F3gOR8p3EKyoWjKZ","name":"Gathering Folklore","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eEverybody knows something about @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.zR5oyR4ZccCyWZg2]{Myths}. How much depends on who they are.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eVassals know about their nearest Myth, and its general direction. If it is adjacent to their home then they know its precise location.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThey know Landmarks in their home and neighbouring Hexes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.GaN0dPf1jqeQ8utO]{Knights}\u003cstrong\u003e \u003c/strong\u003eand \u003cstrong\u003eVagabonds\u003c/strong\u003e have roamed enough to know about a random Myth of the Realm and its rough direction. They also know of the nearest @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Fy9hueqdKhEX0zYj]{Landmarks}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAll of the above know \u003cstrong\u003erumours\u003c/strong\u003e that warn of dangers, but not how to avoid or undo them.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.XD4dA6vKjurF4VsY]{Seers} know the \u003cstrong\u003erules\u003c/strong\u003e of all Myths, their secrets, and their locations. They know their weaknesses, and cures to their maladies. They know all Landmarks in the Realm. Such vast knowledge isn’t given freely.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 19\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"y6kKETT9xRDyK2qW","name":"Getting Started","pages":[{"_id":"AQyRRyNBXuOt9NDq","name":"Getting Started","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eOne player is the Referee. They should read through to the end of the rules section.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe other players can go straight to the @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Md0zQN9AtzRsos3i]{Knighthood} page and need not read any further unless curious.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNext: @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.hkdvxbEDAI7rM6wc]{Start \u0026amp; Scope}\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 6\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"uRBBp89wHoJbxHCD","name":"Giving Information","pages":[{"_id":"bXW6ZMYEpx4RmZa3","name":"Giving Information","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eThe players can only make interesting choices when they are presented with difficult situations and given all of the information needed to engage with them.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 16\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"p1BbrqwB3IL5KnsP","name":"Glory","pages":[{"_id":"9fzC0mcZuUz4xHBJ","name":"Glory","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eAll Knights seek Glory, that they might one day be deemed worthy of the City Quest.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eGLORY THROUGH MYTHS\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen the group feels that a Myth has been resolved, reaching a conclusion of any type, all Knights who played a part in that Myth gain 1 Glory.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eGLORY BY OTHER MEANS\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn a public duel or joust, Knights may stake Glory against a willing opponent. The victor gains 1 Glory, the loser loses 1 Glory.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTournaments may also grant 1 Glory to the winning Knight, provided there are significant spectators and spectacle.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf a battle is large enough to be remembered in history, all Knights on the victorious side gain 1 Glory.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen the game moves to a new Age all Knights gain 1 Glory through serving the Realm and manoeuvring in Court.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eRANK\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eA Knight’s Glory dictates their rank:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e0 Glory - Knight-Errant\u003cbr /\u003eWorthy of leading a Warband\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e3 Glory - Knight-Gallant\u003cbr /\u003eWorthy of a seat in Council or Court\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e6 Glory - Knight-Tenant\u003cbr /\u003eWorthy of ruling a Holding\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e9 Glory - Knight-Dominant\u003cbr /\u003eWorthy of ruling a Seat of Power\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e12 Glory - Knight-Radiant\u003cbr /\u003eWorthy of the City Quest\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 6\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"knKOaTnN5txOVdIh","name":"Grand Designs","pages":[{"_id":"QgV4Xi6VJ2R6tp7E","name":"Grand Designs","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eWork on existing buildings or infrastructure is generally completed by the next @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.BuleIJa3bFxPopzQ]{Season}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew buildings or infrastructure can be completed in a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.BuleIJa3bFxPopzQ]{Season}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eGrand projects such as castles and roads require an entire @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.9btBt0rE5AvXw3mt]{Age} of work.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 21\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"oY1Asu19v9iHa8zw","name":"Guard (GD)","pages":[{"_id":"LCU9rxfBMP3hkkSp","name":"Guard (GD)","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003eGuard\u003c/b\u003e (\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eGD\u003c/span\u003e) is your skill at avoiding Wounds.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen a target is damaged, the damage is first deducted from their GD.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 7\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"UuZ3UFDChYMN7gTh","name":"Hazards","pages":[{"_id":"AUwFqIRETR8BFYBv","name":"Hazards","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eNature fights every step. Devise a solution, push through (lose [[/r d6]] in a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.a3wuqgFMQEMjrm0S]{Virtue}, usually \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003e), or go back the way you came.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 14\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"xClo9CbpoanGqoav","name":"Hefty","pages":[{"_id":"Ix9PaxmU2TSlNw7c","name":"Hefty","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eHefty weapons require one hand. Only one Hefty item can be wielded at once.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"dJeZTvmudZnjrS96","name":"Holdings","pages":[{"_id":"aEUs5TZi0JaFavgH","name":"Holdings","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eHoldings are typically castles, walled towns, fortresses, or towers, held by Knights or influential Vassals. Most of the @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.3hsMdqsglAWNjUQu]{Realm} lives within their walls or the surrounding Hex.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOne holding in each realm is @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.ml5gCjU1JAnzXajw]{The Seat of Power}. This is the Holding of the ruler of the whole Realm, commonly a Knight.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 14\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"LF2qgzMQLIFvnyy4","name":"Hospitality","pages":[{"_id":"tBzPN1C2wccb7Yrx","name":"Hospitality","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eWhen sleeping indoors, do not make a Wilderness Roll. Manners dictate that hospitality be granted to travelling Knights. Longer stays warrant a favour in return.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 18\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"w0AdMBWGQLWhQHd8","name":"Impaired","pages":[{"_id":"cFs9WCNBWfTJH6G7","name":"Impaired","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eImpaired\u003c/strong\u003e attacks roll d4 only and cannot gain bonus dice or benefit from Feats.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 8\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"JowbBiXQHAfcJjy9","name":"Improvisation","pages":[{"_id":"pSWxhAShbMgYdjKj","name":"Improvisation","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eWhen faced with a question not answered by rules, notes, or procedures, you improvise.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAnything too beneficial or too harmful creates the feeling of an arbitrary world. Instead, describe something that does at least one of the following:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEvokes\u003c/strong\u003e the flavour and themes of the area and its inhabitants.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIndulges\u003c/strong\u003e their senses. Vision, hearing, touch, smell, and taste.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReinforces\u003c/strong\u003e something that they\u0027ve already learned about this place.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 16\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"Md0zQN9AtzRsos3i","name":"Knighthood","pages":[{"_id":"sYw9JP9hq05tBZAL","name":"Knighthood","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eYou are Knights, united by a common Oath and visions of the City. You may have dreams of glory, but every Knight must accept the risk of death.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Seers who knighted you have deemed that you travel as a Company. While some of you may rest, roam, or die, your collective journey will be as one.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eKnights have 3 @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.a3wuqgFMQEMjrm0S]{Virtues}. Roll a value for each in order. The Start that you chose for your Company determines the dice you roll. If unsure, roll [[/r d12+d6]].\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003eOUR\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eStrong limbs, firm hands, powerful lungs.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eCLA\u003c/span\u003eRITY\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eKeen instinct, lucid mind, shrewd eyes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eSPI\u003c/span\u003eRIT\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eCharming tongue, iron will, fierce heart.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eRoll for @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.oY1Asu19v9iHa8zw]{Guard (\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eGD\u003c/span\u003e)}, your skill at avoiding Wounds. The Start that you chose for your Company determines the dice you roll. If unsure, roll [[/r d6]].\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eRoll ([[/r 1d6+1d12]]) or choose a Knight.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis gives:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProperty\u003c/strong\u003e: Items brought with you.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAbility\u003c/strong\u003e: A special talent unique to you.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePassion\u003c/strong\u003e: A special means you have to restore your Spirit.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEvery Knight has a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.QCO3X6n1tHqez2DV]{Dagger} ([[/r d6]]), torches, rope, dry rations, and camping gear.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEvery Knight knows the three @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Ii4ZqGwzc3qZWA8B]{Feats}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEvery Knight has sworn the Oath:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSEEK THE MYTHS\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHONOUR THE SEERS\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePROTECT THE REALM\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 7\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"GaN0dPf1jqeQ8utO","name":"Knights","pages":[{"_id":"ebFXKrCD56A6daXZ","name":"Knights","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThose who take the Oath are held in esteem, but expectations burden them.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThey rely on their arms, but are expected to know the customs of peace.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUsually one Knight holds each title, passed on in retirement or death\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eEach Knight can be used for a player character or non-player Knights who are encountered wandering or ruling. Generally each player should have a different type of Knight.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSome Realms refer to Knights by honorific titles and ranks, others their given name and home, while most use their full knightly title or simply \u0026ldquo;Knight.\u0026rdquo;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 13 and 26\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"Fy9hueqdKhEX0zYj","name":"Landmarks","pages":[{"_id":"iXjQcaZmY294Z0nY","name":"Landmarks","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eSome Wilderness Hexes contain a Landmark. These are discovered when travellers roll 4-6 on the Wilderness roll. A typical Realm has 3 or 4 of each type of Landmark.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEven characters who know a Landmark’s location must still make a Wilderness Roll to check for Omens as they travel there.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEach Landmark type covers a range of specific features, with prompts provided on Knight and Myth pages in the book.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe course of the game may create new Landmarks or remove or alter existing ones.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe 6 types of landmarks are:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.gEhHqMT5ciuQNZXm]{Dwellings}\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.QWZ5Xsa3vuo5Bf69]{Sanctums}\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.lBdvsLmaxCzXExnv]{Monuments}\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.UuZ3UFDChYMN7gTh]{Hazards}\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.ihrxnfnNnK4x8KPd]{Curses}\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.TuBkbx1jAFCmrp19]{Ruins}\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 14\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"WulWegthfVVDtzTM","name":"Lay of the Land","pages":[{"_id":"951Do06BzSEimM7z","name":"Lay of the Land","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eEach Hex is large and diverse, a land within the land. Some may spend their whole lives within one. A forest Hex might have cliffs, streams, clearings, and caves.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eUse Spark Tables and the prompts at the base of each Knight and Myth spread to help fill the blanks in your Hexes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 19\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"CgKQNnZcpB6U2J3K","name":"Local Mood","pages":[{"_id":"KcQNfcMjIqgUEjN8","name":"Local Mood","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eWhen arriving in a Holding, roll to gauge the local mood.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"64\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e[[/r 1d6]]\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ch3\u003eLOCAL MOOD\u003c/h3\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"64\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e1\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eOccupied by a looming or recent \u003cstrong\u003ewoe\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"64\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e2-3\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eThere is a sense of things in \u003cstrong\u003edecline\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"64\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e4-6\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eA \u003cstrong\u003efine mood\u003c/strong\u003e and all seems well enough.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 18\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"zs2bGjpkII2Etmnv","name":"Long","pages":[{"_id":"zLTqmwt8zwqs85xC","name":"Long","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eLong weapons require both hands and are @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.w0AdMBWGQLWhQHd8]{Impaired} in confined environments.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"N33evafMmtu93930","name":"Luck Rolls","pages":[{"_id":"TUEeLzsLqhhkP7ev","name":"Luck Rolls","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eIf you need to consult the whims of fate, make a Luck Roll on a d6. A high roll favours the players, a low one does not.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn general, use these guidelines:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e[[/r 1d6]]\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ch3\u003eLUCK ROLL\u003c/h3\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e1\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCrisis:\u003c/strong\u003e Something immediately bad.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e2-3\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProblem:\u003c/strong\u003e Something potentially bad.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e4-6\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBlessing: \u003c/strong\u003eA welcome result.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 16\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"88tV0IZ35JoGJ2bt","name":"Minor Actions","pages":[{"_id":"0qCKlUrsoW55aB0x","name":"Minor Actions","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eChanging weapons, dismounting, and similar actions do not count as a combatant’s action for the turn.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 8\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"T74kT3xY6yPC3MK2","name":"Misrule","pages":[{"_id":"8h2Zd2R2PeiTzTSC","name":"Misrule","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eIf a season ends with 3 or more unresolved @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.VKF3X9roMxCO2nPp]{Crises} then the @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Ht6YdS1x8Va8s16q]{Domain} goes into misrule. Vassals revolt, Knights leave, and pretenders move in on their claims.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 20\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"lBdvsLmaxCzXExnv","name":"Monuments","pages":[{"_id":"wZiOKd4CVH2yf95d","name":"Monuments","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eSites of inspiration. Travellers may spend a Phase to restore \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eSPI\u003c/span\u003e here as if they were consuming a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.B2owmLXQ62SX30oD]{Sacrament}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 14\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"Kkozior5c3JbSn39","name":"Mortal Wounds","pages":[{"_id":"TJ536J8HtWQVHjtR","name":"Mortal Wounds","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eIf a character is struck and loses half or more of their remaining \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003e it is a mortal wound\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMortally Wounded targets are down and dying. They die if left untended for an hour, but can be patched up in a few moments.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 8\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"arw6LSD4H5hvFDS3","name":"Mounted Combat","pages":[{"_id":"BXEV1MfqehycoMGC","name":"Mounted Combat","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eMounted combatants use their steed’s trample Damage in addition to their own weapons when charging enemies on foot. This doesn’t work against spearwalls. Steeds can be targeted separately by attacks.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eBeing dismounted causes [[/r 1d6]] Damage. If this occurs in combat, add it to the existing dice.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"fugS9PjneIggcHrs","name":"Mustering Troops","pages":[{"_id":"IlN9f4lY7j0elaaL","name":"Mustering Troops","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eA typical @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.ml5gCjU1JAnzXajw]{Seat of Power} can muster 3 @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.IemxfFfJIeEBZp2e]{Warbands}, other Holdings 2. The @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.cQMFWOJXOBNZTa5w]{The Marshal} determines their training and armament.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 21\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"UkLl5Nh8ALo2rOgs","name":"Myth Hexes","pages":[{"_id":"PV9jTe4t3aykahPM","name":"Myth Hexes","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eEnding a phase in the Hex containing a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.zR5oyR4ZccCyWZg2]{Myth} always reveals its next @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.T3loxnAcV5W8mGZz]{Omen} without making a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.PxSDkx5wU6kRX5V3]{Wilderness Roll}. When possible, the Knights also get the drop on the Omen.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 18\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"zR5oyR4ZccCyWZg2","name":"Myths","pages":[{"_id":"i378lpYyXgqmtDjo","name":"Myths","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eStories that became truths, or are destined to come to pass.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eNobody agrees on the details, but every version is true in some way.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThere’s no such thing as “just a myth”.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eEach Myth lists its Omens and the cast of beings who are associated with it.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEntering or exploring the Myth\u0027s Hex always reveals its next Omen, remembering @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.XNvXhLKSGgqDI8uD]{Primacy of Action}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Hex itself is visually tied to the Myth\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen the group feels that a Myth is resolved the Knights each gain 1 Glory and a new Myth replaces it in the next Season.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMyths may appear at odds with their Realm, such as The Sea in a desert.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eStill, these Myths must be brought to pass, so Realm and Myth can shift as needed.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 13 and 27\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"T3loxnAcV5W8mGZz","name":"Omens","pages":[{"_id":"ljD0A2ppKJpLnMd5","name":"Omens","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eEach Myth has 6 Omens, listed in the order in which they are encountered. The first encounter with a specific Myth is always Omen 1, the second Omen 2 etc.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eRemember @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.XNvXhLKSGgqDI8uD]{Primacy of Action}. If the players want to hunt for the Wyvern’s nest they don’t have to wait for that Omen to appear if they take action themselves.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 18\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"6xdhNEX7Ptw9GiO6","name":"Phases of the Day","pages":[{"_id":"q2Gtn8i94EAoLfHV","name":"Phases of the Day","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eEach \u003cstrong\u003eDay\u003c/strong\u003e has 3 \u003cstrong\u003ePhases\u003c/strong\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMorning\u003c/strong\u003e: Sunrise to Noon.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAfternoon\u003c/strong\u003e: Noon to Sunset.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNight\u003c/strong\u003e: Sunset to Sunrise.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 17\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"XNvXhLKSGgqDI8uD","name":"Primacy of Action","pages":[{"_id":"s9uD1qDSV9QIBcir","name":"Primacy of Action","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eEven when using the rules for travel, exploration, and combat, remember this, the most important thing:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePast action taken by the players supersedes content generated by prompts or rules. Their deeds are reality.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eRemember the core of giving players information, honouring their choices, and describing the impact of their actions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 16\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"nnTyx6kp0UQOfZFa","name":"Prompts","pages":[{"_id":"iEaXxnnyQhxde9FW","name":"Prompts","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eEvery Knight and Myth spread has prompts across its base. These serve as cues for improvisation as needed. Spark Tables\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eare also useful for generating ideas.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 16\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"sC5DFwEuA3qy9sYa","name":"Ranged Combat","pages":[{"_id":"almRApwRkdoVKNBy","name":"Ranged Combat","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003ePurely ranged weapons cannot be used if the attacker is engaged-in or began their turn in melee.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eProtective cover grants an additional point of Armour against ranged attacks.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ZIhAfEIJGxPSkupp","name":"Reaction","pages":[{"_id":"37XpVI1wRRVrLKGW","name":"Reaction","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eNon-player characters react in a way that feels appropriate for the current context.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen uncertain, a character makes a \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eSPI\u003c/span\u003e Save to avoid an unfavourable reaction.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 8\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"3hsMdqsglAWNjUQu","name":"Realms","pages":[{"_id":"5BFTz8PyJQyMGmey","name":"Realms","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe world is fractured into petty Realms, each ruled from a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.ml5gCjU1JAnzXajw]{Seat of Power}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSmaller @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.dJeZTvmudZnjrS96]{Holdings}are walled settlements tended by Vassals, guarded by Knights.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMost that lies between is wilderness.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 13\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"bmaKPUz2FBGCgBIt","name":"Recovery","pages":[{"_id":"FZK6oQg5Nx9Z8rZz","name":"Recovery","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.oY1Asu19v9iHa8zw]{Guard} is fully restored with just a moment of peace after the danger has passed.\u003cbr /\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.h4ATNWH8WwUmQNdC]{Fatigue} is also removed this way.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVirtues\u003c/strong\u003e can be fully restored by 3 means:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eConsuming a specific type of @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.VwJ2aV2jxvFuXhL0]{Remedy}\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePerforming a specific Action\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSkipping to a new Season\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eVigour is restored by consuming @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.04y6tu0NjqOtOxHU]{Sustenance} or spending a full day in warm hospitality.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eClarity is restored by consuming @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.m4eN8wzWx1wIP2mK]{Stimulant} or receiving guidance from a Seer.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSpirit is restored by consuming @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.B2owmLXQ62SX30oD]{Sacrament}or indulging a Passion.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 9\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"AtE3VDow2oyGnBK7","name":"Roles","pages":[{"_id":"MplJEhRFz4rtktwe","name":"Roles","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMost fall into one of four roles: Vassal, Vagabond, Knight, or Seer. A web of seniority exists within and between each.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eVassals serve a ruler, typically a Knight, in return for protection.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eVagabonds roam, working for and protecting only themselves.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 13\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"TuBkbx1jAFCmrp19","name":"Ruins","pages":[{"_id":"LT7ZHosOskZmh3ni","name":"Ruins","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eRemnants of the past echo the future. These hint at a random Myth not currently active in the Realm, though it may return.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 14\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"Ht6YdS1x8Va8s16q","name":"Ruling a Domain","pages":[{"_id":"WUdJeGICKsMbE3Hm","name":"Ruling a Domain","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eIn return for pledging loyalty to @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.ml5gCjU1JAnzXajw]{The Seat of Power}, a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.dJeZTvmudZnjrS96]{Holding} might be granted to a Knight or influential Vassal. This forms a Domain. Wilderness Hexes and their @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Fy9hueqdKhEX0zYj]{Landmarks} formally fall under the dominion of their nearest Holding.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 20\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"QWZ5Xsa3vuo5Bf69","name":"Sanctums","pages":[{"_id":"gd9eIMu9fgF8t34h","name":"Sanctums","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eEach Sanctum is the sacred home to a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.XD4dA6vKjurF4VsY]{Seer}. Roll on the Knight table, consulting their page to discover which Seer.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 14\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"gTEIj7A03CsV7ChK","name":"Saves","pages":[{"_id":"77uilofFn57JnA6G","name":"Saves","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eTo pass a Save, roll a [[/r d20]] equal or below the relevant @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.a3wuqgFMQEMjrm0S]{Virtue}. Failure means negative consequences, not always a failed action.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 8\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"sc76aTlM7OLBPigZ","name":"Scars","pages":[{"_id":"5TTqKpLcKmJ9GCsh","name":"Scars","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eTake the die that caused the Scar and roll it again, consulting the table below for the specific Scar caused.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eVirtue Loss through Scars is not Damage, so cannot Mortally Wound or Slay the victim.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eScars are only gained through real, deadly combat, not training or bloodless duels.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eScar\u003c/h3\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"76\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e1\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDistress\u003c/strong\u003e – \u003cem\u003eA lucky escape Lose d6 \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eSPI\u003c/span\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"76\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e2\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDisfigurement\u003c/strong\u003e – \u003cem\u003eA permanent mark\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/em\u003eRoll [[/r 1d6]]:\u003cbr /\u003e1: Eye, 2: Cheek, 3: Neck,\u003cbr /\u003e4: Torso, 5: Nose, 6: Jaw.\u003cbr /\u003eIf your max \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eGD\u003c/span\u003e is 2 or less, increase it by [[/r d6]].\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"76\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e3\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSmash\u003c/strong\u003e – \u003cem\u003eA sudden spray of blood\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/em\u003eLose [[/r d6]] \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"76\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e4\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStun\u003c/strong\u003e – \u003cem\u003ePain drowns the senses\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/em\u003eLose [[/r d6]] \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eCLA\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eIf your max GD is 4 or less, increase it by [[/r d6]].\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"76\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e5\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRupture\u003c/strong\u003e – \u003cem\u003eInnards pierced and compressed\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/em\u003eLose [[/r 2d6]] VIG.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"76\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e6\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGouge\u003c/strong\u003e – \u003cem\u003eFlesh torn from bone\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/em\u003eWhen you get stitched up, if your max GD is 6 or less, increase it by [[/r d6]].\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"76\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e7\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConcussion\u003c/strong\u003e – \u003cem\u003eA heavy blow numbs the mind\u003c/em\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eLose [[/r 2d6]] CLA.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"76\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e8\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTear\u003c/strong\u003e – \u003cem\u003eSomething taken in violent struggle\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/em\u003eRoll [[/r 1d6]]:\u003cbr /\u003e1: Nose, 2: Ear, 3: Finger,\u003cbr /\u003e4: Thumb, 5: Eye, 6: Chunk of Scalp.\u003cbr /\u003eWhen you get patched up, if your max GD is 8 or less, increase it by [[/r 1d6]].\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"76\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e9\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAgony\u003c/strong\u003e – \u003cem\u003eWith a crack, a torturous break\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/em\u003eLose [[/r 2d6]] SPI.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"76\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e10\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMutilation\u003c/strong\u003e – \u003cem\u003eA limb rendered lost or useless\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/em\u003eRoll [[/r 1d6]]:\u003cbr /\u003e1-2: Leg, 3-4: Shield Arm, 5-6: Sword Arm.\u003cbr /\u003eBy next Season you have a prosthetic or have learned to get by, and if your max GD is 10 or less, increase it by [[/r d6]].\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"76\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e11\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDoom\u003c/strong\u003e – \u003cem\u003eA cheated death haunts you\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you take a Mortal Wound this Season you are Slain instead.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"76\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e12\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHumiliation\u003c/strong\u003e – \u003cem\u003eA most dolorous stroke\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen you achieve revenge, if your max GD is 12 or less, increase it by [[/r d6]].\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 9\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"NHGNkjkhMijIw4C0","name":"Scopes","pages":[{"_id":"8k0bbqdxipnE6niS","name":"Scopes","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAdventure\u003c/strong\u003e - One session. Here it can save time to generate a few Knights ahead of the game and let the players choose one each.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eChronicle\u003c/strong\u003e - A known number of sessions. Season and Age turns are planned out ahead of time. For six sessions this might be a Season turn at the end of each session, and an Age turn at the end of each Winter.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSaga\u003c/strong\u003e - An indeterminate number of sessions. Here you can let the players guide the scope as they explore the world.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 6\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"sTvugWMrpC0o4dpF","name":"Searching","pages":[{"_id":"Kgo5bWChbkie3iaX","name":"Searching","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eIt takes a whole @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.6xdhNEX7Ptw9GiO6]{Phase} to carry out a surface level sweep of an entire Hex, thoroughly search for something known to exist there, or find a vantage point.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 19\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"BuleIJa3bFxPopzQ","name":"Seasons","pages":[{"_id":"n66fEMEZxA8KxQe4","name":"Seasons","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eEach \u003cstrong\u003eYear\u003c/strong\u003e has 3 \u003cstrong\u003eSeasons\u003c/strong\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSpring\u003c/strong\u003e - \u003cem\u003eThe Green Season\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBegins with the Feast of the Sun, a day of excess and revelry to strengthen both the people and the land.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMidspring sees Sceptremass, where @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.ml5gCjU1JAnzXajw]{The Seat of Power} gathers local rulers to renew their vows of loyalty.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEnds with the Tax, a share of coins collected by the Realm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHarvest\u003c/strong\u003e - \u003cem\u003eThe Gold Season\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBegins with the Feast of the Stars, a night of honours, unions, and contests.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMidharvest sees Eldermass, a secretive assembly of Seers and trusted associates.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEnds with the Tithe, a share of food and drink collected by the Realm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWinter\u003c/strong\u003e - \u003cem\u003eThe Grey Season\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBegins with the Feast of the Moon, a solemn reflection of mortality and history.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMidwinter sees Kindlemass, a sacred day of warmth and goodwill, where each home must open their doors to all.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEnds with the Levy, a share of materials and crafted goods collected by the Realm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 17\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"XD4dA6vKjurF4VsY","name":"Seers","pages":[{"_id":"LboKvQv5ooKstlzg","name":"Seers","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThose who understand the nature of @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.zR5oyR4ZccCyWZg2]{Myth} enough to glimpse into our future.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eTheir visions grant legitimacy and direction to a Knight’s quest.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThey know when a Squire is ready to become a Knight, and when a Knight is ready to seek the City.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 13\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"pl9IZBYdgdk404En","name":"Services","pages":[{"_id":"GoQDXQgfmCLVtdyR","name":"Services","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.dJeZTvmudZnjrS96]{Holdings} house a range of people who can be called on for service. The larger the Holding, the more likely that a particular service is being offered there.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMany will gladly offer their service to a Knight, but all have limits, after which they ask something in return or refuse entirely.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs with trade, the key question comes down to “What can I offer that they would value?”.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCommon\u003c/strong\u003e services are offered everywhere.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUncommon\u003c/strong\u003e services require training.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRare\u003c/strong\u003e services require a lifetime dedication.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eRoll their @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.a3wuqgFMQEMjrm0S]{Virtues} on [[/r d12+d6]]\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eCOMMON\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eServant\u003c/strong\u003e: 2\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eGD\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSingle duty with little expertise\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGuide\u003c/strong\u003e: 4GD\u003cbr /\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.xlZaXdsyxCP8E9XI]{Handaxe}([[/r d6]]), @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.pFEsSqdFQyjEU1pN]{Javelin}([[/r d6]]), local knowledge\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSentry: 3GD\u003cbr /\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.VE7vXdiy1TmoNMFH]{Billhook}([[/r d10]] long), little appetite for combat\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eUNCOMMON\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHerbalist\u003c/strong\u003e: 2GD\u003cbr /\u003eKnows treatments, not cures\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSoldier-at-Arms\u003c/strong\u003e: 6GD\u003cbr /\u003eA2 (@UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.UtHKYmeBDzrFdDXz]{Helm}, @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.8QKLl6QqDFbxRwUf]{Shield})\u003cbr /\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.bhH83HZyRwBOqLhd]{Spear}([[/r d6]] hefty), @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.8QKLl6QqDFbxRwUf]{Shield}([[/r d4]]), battle worn\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eArcher\u003c/strong\u003e: 3GD\u003cbr /\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.hjVEH81r0j5AZIqx]{Shortbow} ([[/r d6]] @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.zs2bGjpkII2Etmnv]{Long})\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eRARE\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSage\u003c/strong\u003e: 2GD\u003cbr /\u003eHolds immense knowledge in a particular\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003earea of expertise\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAlchemist\u003c/strong\u003e: 2GD\u003cbr /\u003eCreates poisons or quasi-medicinal potions\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSellsword\u003c/strong\u003e: 7GD\u003cbr /\u003eA4 (@UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.AkIZO3pU7XrTzJK2]{Coat}, @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.MgrxzDhulacjitl0]{Plates}, @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.UtHKYmeBDzrFdDXz]{Helm}, @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.8QKLl6QqDFbxRwUf]{Shield})\u003cbr /\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.DJt25tLqpGviWbYn]{Longsword} ([[/r 2d8]] @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.xClo9CbpoanGqoav]{Hefty}), @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.8QKLl6QqDFbxRwUf]{Shield} ([[/r d4]])\u003cbr /\u003eGenerally only agrees to fights that they are confident they can win\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 13\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"iTdwOrgq47EPbkJq","name":"Shieldwalls \u0026 Spearwalls","pages":[{"_id":"JYnsLU8aRShCRrEN","name":"Shieldwalls \u0026 Spearwalls","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e3 or more allies may form a wall formation. If they all bear shields (not bucklers) then they gain an additional point of Armour. If they all bear spears (or similar) then enemies cannot Attack on the turn that they *charge.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e*Charge means \"move into contact then attack in melee\" \u003ca href=\"https://discord.com/channels/499193406828838922/1395010166856089683/1396764738687602790\"\u003e\u003cbr/\u003e- Chris McDowell on Discord, 7/21/2025\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"uPLF8utwanQWOLvz","name":"Ships \u0026 Structures","pages":[{"_id":"ZpO3eR4CZ2NbFU8t","name":"Ships \u0026 Structures","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003ch3\u003eWOOD AND STONE\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eShips and structures are destroyed at 0\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eGD\u003c/span\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eRecovering GD takes a day of repairs.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWooden\u003c/strong\u003e structures and ships ignore Attacks other than from fire, siege weapons, or suitably large creatures.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStone\u003c/strong\u003e walls cannot be breached by conventional means, though their gates are usually a viable target.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eGate: 5GD, A2\u003cbr /\u003eRampart: 10GD, A2\u003cbr /\u003eCastle Wall: 10GD, A3\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eColliding ships take d12 Damage. If one ship is much larger it takes d6 Damage instead.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eRowboat: 4GD, carries 6 passengers\u003cbr /\u003eLongship: 7GD, A1, carries a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.IemxfFfJIeEBZp2e]{Warband}\u003cbr /\u003eWarship: 10GD, A2, carries 2 @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.IemxfFfJIeEBZp2e]{Warbands}\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eARTILLERY AND SIEGERY\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eSiege Tower: 7GD, A2\u003cbr /\u003eBattering Ram: [[/r d12]]\u003cbr /\u003eStone Thrower: [[/r d12]] @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Q84GshhKtznJytyY]{Blast}\u003cbr /\u003eBolt Launcher: [[/r 2d12]]\u003cbr /\u003eTrebuchet: [[/r 3d12]] @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Q84GshhKtznJytyY]{Blast}, immobile\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 11\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"mTCLJfKpbMHmQUaN","name":"Sites","pages":[{"_id":"rvJY5YJvFgZlgclh","name":"Sites","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eA Knight’s journey largely focuses on travelling great distances to seek the guidance of Seers and uncover Myths.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eHowever, on occasion there may be the need to zoom in on a single Hex, or a specific site within a Hex, in more detail.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSites can be created as areas that warrant more detailed exploration, whether ancient tombs, hostile castles, twisting caverns, or misty woods spanning the entire Hex.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhile they can be plotted out with any number of traditional methods, this is a quick Hex-based method.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003ePOINTS AND ROUTES\u003c/h3\u003e\u003col\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDraw 6 points as the corners of a hexagon, with a 7th in the centre.\u003c/p\u003e\u003col\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMark 3 points with circles. These are \u003cstrong\u003efeatures\u003c/strong\u003e that give information or set the mood.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMark 2 with triangles. These are \u003cstrong\u003edangers\u003c/strong\u003e to be navigated carefully.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMark 1 with a diamond. This is \u003cstrong\u003etreasure\u003c/strong\u003e, a useful or valuable find.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eErase the final point and assign numbers to the remaining points.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eNeighbouring points can be connected by three types of route.\u003c/p\u003e\u003col\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDraw 3 \u003cstrong\u003eopen\u003c/strong\u003e routes with a solid line. These are straightforward paths between points.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDraw 2 \u003cstrong\u003eclosed\u003c/strong\u003e routes with a crossed line. Here something blocks the way, so creative thinking is required.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDraw 1 \u003cstrong\u003ehidden\u003c/strong\u003e route with a dotted line. This path is only found through specific exploration of its connecting points or local knowledge.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMake sure all points can be reached, even if one of the routes is closed or secret.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf applicable, place an entrance in any point, and an optional hidden entrance.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003ch3\u003eBREAKING THE RULES\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe guidelines on this page are just a starting point. Rearrange the distribution of the types of point, route, and entrance if it suits the theme of the site better.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSo a sealed burial complex might have:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePoints: 3 Treasures, 2 Dangers, 1 Feature\u003cbr /\u003eRoutes: 3 Closed, 2 Secret, 1 Open\u003cbr /\u003eEntrances: 1 Entrance only\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 15\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"V0M3WNBrV1pQB3Xi","name":"Sleep","pages":[{"_id":"Wt6zXVBsgB3ZIffn","name":"Sleep","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eEach morning, all who did not get proper sleep the previous day lose [[/r d6]] \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eCLA\u003c/span\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 18\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"TL8avk3aIUjFozBV","name":"Slow","pages":[{"_id":"PEJ7WQPeshZN7Jtx","name":"Slow","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eSlow weapons cannot be used if the attacker has moved this turn. They are also @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.zs2bGjpkII2Etmnv]{Long}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"w5kp8Mu6RhZosdcq","name":"Smite","pages":[{"_id":"MadQ2sYdvnClHW8e","name":"Smite","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eRelease your righteous fury\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eUse before rolling a melee Attack.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Attack gains either +[[/r d12]]or @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Q84GshhKtznJytyY]{Blast}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePass a \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003e Save or become Fatigued.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"iErvWGTiHxk2AKKA","name":"Squires","pages":[{"_id":"l6QYTwHQMb60AaI7","name":"Squires","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eSmall Companies (2 Knights or fewer) may give each Knight a Squire. They serve as apprentices, and are not yet Knights, so\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ecannot gain Glory or perform Feats.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e[[/r 2d6]] for each Virtue, 1\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eGD\u003c/span\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThey ride a pony (\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003e 7, \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eCLA\u003c/span\u003e 7, \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eSPI\u003c/span\u003e 2, 2GD) and\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ecarry a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.QCO3X6n1tHqez2DV]{Dagger} ([[/r d6]]).\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eRoll d6 for their extra equipment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1: @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.t0GC5p3EBpIeQWFW]{Cudgel}([[/r d8]] @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.xClo9CbpoanGqoav]{Hefty}),\u003cbr /\u003e2: @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.OaSMuVzXve86aFK2]{Axe}([[/r d8]] @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.xClo9CbpoanGqoav]{Hefty}),\u003cbr /\u003e3: @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.miyMiAJhHRd1auM3]{Hatchet}([[/r d6]]),\u003cbr /\u003e4: @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.hjVEH81r0j5AZIqx]{Shortbow}([[/r d6]] @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.zs2bGjpkII2Etmnv]{Long}),\u003cbr /\u003e5: @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.8QKLl6QqDFbxRwUf]{Shield} ([[/r d4]], A1)\u003cbr /\u003e6: Three @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.pFEsSqdFQyjEU1pN]{Javelins}([[/r d6]]).\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen Knighted they gain [[/r d6]]in each Virtue.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 7\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"aa0Sh1GxlbNwtO1p","name":"Start","pages":[{"_id":"Uzc6CreTY0pF7Zdp","name":"Start","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWanderer\u003c/strong\u003e - Young Knights-Errant with d6\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eGD\u003c/span\u003e (Guard) and [[/r d12+d6]] in each @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.a3wuqgFMQEMjrm0S]{Virtue}. They arrive in the Realm seeking Glory. If they lack direction, have them seek a Seer’s counsel.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCourtier\u003c/strong\u003e - Mature Knights-Gallant with [[/r 2d6]]GD and [[/r d12+6]] (six, not d6) in each @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.a3wuqgFMQEMjrm0S]{Virtue}. They have a place in Court at the Seat of Power. The first Omen of the nearest Myth is delivered as news to the Court.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRuler\u003c/strong\u003e - Mature Knights-Tenant with [[/r d6+6]]GD and [[/r d12+6]] (six, not d6) in each @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.a3wuqgFMQEMjrm0S]{Virtue}. One Knight rules a Holding, the others are in their Circle. The Seat of Power is under a wicked influence.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 6\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"hkdvxbEDAI7rM6wc","name":"Start \u0026 Scope","pages":[{"_id":"Zmy3jMzhKPh78TM9","name":"Start \u0026 Scope","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eEvery group that sits down to play the game is different, and you should consider the Start and Scope of a game before you begin.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.aa0Sh1GxlbNwtO1p]{Start}\u003c/strong\u003e is the opening situation in which the players find themselves. The \u003cstrong\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.NHGNkjkhMijIw4C0]{Scope}\u003c/strong\u003e is how long you expect the game to run for, both in and out of game.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 6\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"g0Pybiito1VevwT3","name":"Succession","pages":[{"_id":"1mByy7lQz2Vt8VNN","name":"Succession","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eTypically a ruler names their successor, though some @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.3hsMdqsglAWNjUQu]{Realms} defer the decision to a conclave of @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.XD4dA6vKjurF4VsY]{Seers} or a group of specially chosen Knights-Elector.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhoever the successor, they are sure to face at least some resistance, and should quickly establish their own authority.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 21\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"SM0nO3IJlpTHc9Ry","name":"Supplies","pages":[{"_id":"KY4xIZA4LddVsIwP","name":"Supplies","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eWhen sleeping outdoors make a  @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.PxSDkx5wU6kRX5V3]{Wilderness Roll} as normal, ignoring @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Fy9hueqdKhEX0zYj]{Landmarks}. Hostile Omens prevent proper sleep, while others may not occur at all if they are improbable as nighttime activity.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 18\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ve87kfCyVMdHYOXp","name":"Surprise","pages":[{"_id":"nGX0rJRYwtYYFCk3","name":"Surprise","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003ePlayers normally take the first turn of combat, discussing their plan and acting in any order they wish.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eCharacters who were not readied for combat must pass a \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eCLA\u003c/span\u003e Save or miss the first turn.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 8\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"CpEsC8mNtdQJspUw","name":"Taxes, Tithes \u0026 Levies","pages":[{"_id":"CpKbf58CifX5RdSi","name":"Taxes, Tithes \u0026 Levies","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eStandard collections keep the @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Ht6YdS1x8Va8s16q]{Domain}running without too much strain. A @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.cQMFWOJXOBNZTa5w]{Steward} can squeeze more from their Vassals for a war or great project, but must roll:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e[[/r d6]]\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ch3\u003eINCREASED COLLECTIONS\u003c/h3\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e1\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eImmediate @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.T74kT3xY6yPC3MK2]{Misrule}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e2-3\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eYour coffers are filled, but take a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.VKF3X9roMxCO2nPp]{Crisis}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e4-6\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Vassals \u003cstrong\u003epay willingly\u003c/strong\u003e, mostly.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 21\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"cQMFWOJXOBNZTa5w","name":"The Council","pages":[{"_id":"JnmA7aVZaOk1aVEU","name":"The Council","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003ePrestigious seats must be filled for a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Ht6YdS1x8Va8s16q]{Domain} to run smoothly. Though you may grant and revoke these roles, those who are scorned rarely go quietly.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSteward\u003c/strong\u003e: Ruling in your absence, carrying your authority and the key to the treasury.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMarshal\u003c/strong\u003e: Training and equipping soldiers, mustering them in times of war.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSheriff\u003c/strong\u003e: Monitoring threats within your Realm and even within your walls.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEnvoy\u003c/strong\u003e: Managing neighbours and providing hospitality to visitors.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe Circle\u003c/strong\u003e: Rulers often invite worthy visiting Knights to sit alongside the Council as equals, an ancient tradition.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMembers of your Council can be assigned to tasks. Depending on the scope these could take a Phase, a Week, or a full Season. These are handled just as normal @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.U0cRZvrvdyQCKHy8]{Actions}, with failure typically causing a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.VKF3X9roMxCO2nPp]{Crisis}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 20\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"X1lghTTFxdKGH1z4","name":"The Court","pages":[{"_id":"86WlZcmaqZYBQUOe","name":"The Court","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eThose who serve outside the Council.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRetainers\u003c/strong\u003e: Vassals taken on by individual Council members to aid in their work.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCourtiers\u003c/strong\u003e: Commoners with lesser responsibilities or ceremonial honours, usually holding higher ambitions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePetitioners\u003c/strong\u003e: Representatives from outside of the Court, granted an audience to seek aid, counsel, or justice.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.XD4dA6vKjurF4VsY]{Seers}: Although they live in their Sanctums they occasionally visit Court or send acolytes in their stead.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 20\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"dBonZyygROm4ueJN","name":"The Hex Map","pages":[{"_id":"nAjROSnG4vFNS0nR","name":"The Hex Map","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eA @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.3hsMdqsglAWNjUQu]{Realm} is mapped on a hexagonal grid covering the loose rule of a Seat of Power. A 12x12 grid is typical, whether the Realm is landlocked, coastal, or an island chain.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTypically, players get a copy of the map with @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.dJeZTvmudZnjrS96]{Holdings} and general terrain marked. They cannot see @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.zR5oyR4ZccCyWZg2]{Myths}, @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Fy9hueqdKhEX0zYj]{Landmarks}, and @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.CapdrFIR5fQTiMqQ]{Barriers}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe distance covered by each hexagon is a Hecksleague, commonly called a Hex.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis distance represents a few loose factors:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe area a hill fort can overlook\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe area that guards can patrol in a day\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eA return hike to a neighbouring Hex gets you home before dark\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 14\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ml5gCjU1JAnzXajw","name":"The Seat of Power","pages":[{"_id":"bEwq6xdojQQFW3nX","name":"The Seat of Power","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eThe Seat of Power is the @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.dJeZTvmudZnjrS96]{Holding} of the ruler of a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.3hsMdqsglAWNjUQu]{Realm}, commonly a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.GaN0dPf1jqeQ8utO]{Knight}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 14\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"O5I0nfb10MRtEujg","name":"Trade","pages":[{"_id":"kdaIqJ4ApLJdbwWV","name":"Trade","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eOnly the rich deal in coins. Most trade is an exchange of raw materials, goods, or service. Frequent trades often grow into ongoing pledges of service, cooperation, or protection.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSimply, if you hope to trade you should have a good answer to the question “What can I offer that they would value?”.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCommon\u003c/strong\u003e items are widely available.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUncommon\u003c/strong\u003e items require a specialist.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRare\u003c/strong\u003e items are truly treasured.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"F69orverAgbGvRAj","name":"Trample","pages":[{"_id":"b7NVoISF3Viwz3iH","name":"Trample","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eMounted combatants use their steed’s trample Damage in addition to their own weapons when charging enemies on foot. This doesn’t work against spearwalls.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 10\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"mgiCvLsMUxnxtQRB","name":"Travel Supplies","pages":[{"_id":"4kHLiHK5SyyScg8z","name":"Travel Supplies","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eKnights gather food, water, and firewood as they travel, so these are not tracked. In situations where essential needs are deprived the Company each lose d6 \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003e each morning.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 18\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"PxSDkx5wU6kRX5V3","name":"Travelling","pages":[{"_id":"WUjzIXc5iVzLY3jd","name":"Travelling","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eTravelling consumes a whole Phase of the day and uses one of 3 methods:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTrek\u003c/strong\u003e: 1 Hex on foot or steed.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGallop\u003c/strong\u003e: 2 Hexes on a non-Exhausted steed. The steed loses [[/r d6]] \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCruise\u003c/strong\u003e: 3 Hexes by boat, or by steed on a rarely-found proper road.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen ending a phase in Wilderness, roll:\u003c/p\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e[[/r 1d6]]\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ch3\u003eWILDERNESS ROLL\u003c/h3\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e1\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eEncounter the next Omen from a \u003cstrong\u003erandom Myth\u003c/strong\u003e in this Realm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e2-3\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eEncounter the next Omen from the \u003cstrong\u003enearest Myth.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e4-6\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eEncounter the Hex’s \u003cstrong\u003eLandmark\u003c/strong\u003e. Otherwise \u003cstrong\u003eall clear.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 18\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"730Af1FmIdloG4vY","name":"Travelling Blind","pages":[{"_id":"D6Gnx6SP8ixUYCIe","name":"Travelling Blind","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eTravellers who find themselves roaming without a proper sense of direction, or shrouded by darkness or mist, must roll when they try to move to a new Hex.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"64\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e[[/r 1d6]]\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ch3\u003eTRAVELLING BLIND\u003c/h3\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"64\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e1\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCircle back\u003c/strong\u003e to where you started\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"64\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e2-3\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDrift\u003c/strong\u003e a Hex to the Left (2) or Right (3)\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"64\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e4-6\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eProgress as \u003cstrong\u003eplanned\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 18\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"R05MWXx2HPz3edbL","name":"Travelling at Night","pages":[{"_id":"Ro16pWZ4uU1HAUMR","name":"Travelling at Night","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eTravelling or exploring at night causes the Company to lose [[/r d6]] \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eSPI\u003c/span\u003e each. If they lack a guide and light they are also @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.730Af1FmIdloG4vY]{Travelling Blind}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 18\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"WvbLkPLFdRXNqUDg","name":"Travelling in Winter","pages":[{"_id":"fycm0Ti6RrpgKLF5","name":"Travelling in Winter","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eAnybody camping or travelling at night in Winter loses [[/r d6]] \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003e. Most Realms also risk @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.1awKBfGuG7xMbNIx]{Dire Weather} during Winter.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 18\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"Qq1IJyI2gwt04hUc","name":"Turns","pages":[{"_id":"pOxLsYG9Rov1oqBj","name":"Turns","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eA turn is enough time to Move and then perform an @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.U0cRZvrvdyQCKHy8]{Action}, always in that order.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 8\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"IIcwopNSELGLVF8y","name":"Unarmed Combat","pages":[{"_id":"0bDHBagtWKndDChy","name":"Unarmed Combat","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eUnarmed attacks are @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.w0AdMBWGQLWhQHd8]{Impaired} unless the attacker has suitable natural weapons.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"KbYH76IbID8eQ2XP","name":"Unresolved Situations","pages":[{"_id":"gHvmm1iCt0VXXXpA","name":"Unresolved Situations","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eIf an important situation is left unresolved before moving to the next @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.BuleIJa3bFxPopzQ]{Season} or @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.9btBt0rE5AvXw3mt]{Age}, roll [[/r d6]] to see how it changes:\u003c/p\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"337\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e[[/r 1d6]]\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003ch3\u003eUNRESOLVED SITUATIONS\u003c/h3\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"337\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e1\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eIt goes as \u003cstrong\u003ebad as it could possibly go.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"337\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e2-3\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eIt gets \u003cstrong\u003eworse.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd data-colwidth=\"337\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e4-6\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eIt gets \u003cstrong\u003ebetter.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 17\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"BGSDtZpzTaF6jhId","name":"Virtue Loss","pages":[{"_id":"mAsAJFn2JE9TjOgb","name":"Virtue Loss","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eVirtues may be reduced by means other than Damage, typically referred to as Virtue Loss. In addition to the situations listed in the rules, characters may suffer Virtue Loss as the cost or consequence of an action. This is detailed in the @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.U0cRZvrvdyQCKHy8]{Action Procedure}.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eVictims are only Slain or Mortally Wounded if the Virtue was reduced by Damage, never as a result of Virtue Loss.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003e 0 you are \u003cem\u003eExhausted\u003c/em\u003e and cannot Attack if you have moved this turn.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eCLA\u003c/span\u003e 0 you are \u003cem\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.h9e6V7nLciONrfTO]{Exposed} \u003c/em\u003eand treated as having 0\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eGD\u003c/span\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eSPI\u003c/span\u003e 0 your attacks are \u003cem\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.w0AdMBWGQLWhQHd8]{Impaired} \u003c/em\u003erolling a single d4 only.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 9\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"a3wuqgFMQEMjrm0S","name":"Virtues","pages":[{"_id":"kkZ8t9lCqtJ3JXRw","name":"Virtues","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eKnights have 3 \u003cstrong\u003eVirtues\u003c/strong\u003e. Roll a value for each in order. The Start that you chose for your Company determines the dice you roll. If unsure, roll [[/r d12+d6]].\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eVirtues can be reduced and raised in a number of ways, but can never go higher than 19 or lower than 0.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003eOUR\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eStrong limbs, firm hands, powerful lungs.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eCLA\u003c/span\u003eRITY\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eKeen instinct, lucid mind, shrewd eyes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eSPI\u003c/span\u003eRIT\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/strong\u003eCharming tongue, iron will, fierce heart.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 8\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"SCbu70lcnYlcIayd","name":"Vision","pages":[{"_id":"xM51OY9xV1RHKj8w","name":"Vision","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eFrom a vantage point it’s possible to get an overview of the current Hex and a general sense of what lies in neighbouring hexes, but not specific details.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 19\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"IemxfFfJIeEBZp2e","name":"Warbands","pages":[{"_id":"z9KB412tbUqgeCli","name":"Warbands","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eTwo-dozen or so combatants fighting together are treated as a single Warband.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen they are @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Kkozior5c3JbSn39]{Mortally Wounded} they are routed from the battle.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eVIG\u003c/span\u003e 0 they are wiped out entirely, at \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eSPI\u003c/span\u003e 0 they are broken.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThey are not harmed by individual attacks unless they are @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Q84GshhKtznJytyY]{Blast} attacks or suitably large-scale.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWarband attacks against individuals receive +[[/r d12]] and cause @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.Q84GshhKtznJytyY]{Blast} Damage.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch3\u003eLEADING FROM THE FRONT\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eOne individual within a Warband can add their Attack dice to the Warband’s Attack Roll, leading from the front. If they do, they suffer the same Damage that the Warband does until their next turn.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eWARBANDS\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMilitia\u003c/strong\u003e: VIG 10, \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eCLA\u003c/span\u003e 10, SPI 7, 3\u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eGD\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eCrude polearm ([[/r d8]] @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.zs2bGjpkII2Etmnv]{Long})\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSkirmishers\u003c/strong\u003e: VIG 10, CLA 13, SPI 10, 2GD\u003cbr /\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.hjVEH81r0j5AZIqx]{Shortbow} ([[/r d6]] @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.zs2bGjpkII2Etmnv]{Long})\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMercenaries\u003c/strong\u003e: VIG 13, CLA 10, SPI 10, 4GD\u003cbr /\u003eA3 (mail, helm, shield) @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.bhH83HZyRwBOqLhd]{Spear} ([[/r d8]] @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.xClo9CbpoanGqoav]{Hefty}), @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.8QKLl6QqDFbxRwUf]{Shield} ([[/r d4]])\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRiders\u003c/strong\u003e: VIG 10, CLA 13, SPI 10, 3GD\u003cbr /\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.pFEsSqdFQyjEU1pN]{Javelins} ([[/r d6]]), @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.xlZaXdsyxCP8E9XI]{Handaxe} ([[/r d6]]), steed\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eKnights\u003c/strong\u003e: VIG 13, CLA 10, SPI 13, 5GD A3 (mail, helm, shield)\u003cbr /\u003e@UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.vHG1rH2nEd3Har48]{Mace} ([[/r d8]] @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.xClo9CbpoanGqoav]{Hefty}), @UUID[Compendium.celestus.items.8QKLl6QqDFbxRwUf]{Shield} ([[/r d4]]), charger ([[/r d8]] @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.F69orverAgbGvRAj]{Trample})\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 11\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"h5p2G4Q0lIzmtYqb","name":"Wavering Morale","pages":[{"_id":"FIU9nTS2Li4ssUvo","name":"Wavering Morale","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eIndividuals who are Wounded, or groups who lose half their number, must pass a \u003cspan class=\"virtue\"\u003eSPI\u003c/span\u003e Save to avoid rout or surrender.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOrganised groups roll once using their leader\u0027s SPI. Disorganised groups roll for each individual against their own SPI. This does not affect player characters.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"7N1238s8e5AItkxT","name":"Wearing Armour","pages":[{"_id":"GjJdIyRhER6bCFAk","name":"Wearing Armour","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eOne of each armour type (coat, plates, helm, shield) can be worn at once, combining their armour scores together. Plates and helm are generally not worn outside of battle.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"YIrmFRycBX67jxoc","name":"Wielding Weapons","pages":[{"_id":"yBdjuX7OczXR5fqG","name":"Wielding Weapons","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eIf no type is noted, assume the weapon uses one hand and has no other restrictions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHefty\u003c/strong\u003e weapons require one hand. Only one Hefty item can be wielded at once.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLong\u003c/strong\u003e weapons require both hands and are @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.w0AdMBWGQLWhQHd8]{Impaired} in confined environments.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSlow\u003c/strong\u003e weapons cannot be used if the attacker has moved this turn. They are also Long.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"SrDvqsJ95Zpx1CzL","name":"Wilderness","pages":[{"_id":"5XXFyz4c8Ni9MsAz","name":"Wilderness","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eMost @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.dBonZyygROm4ueJN]{Hexes} are Wilderness, with a variety of terrain types. Spark Tables can help with this. As a general guide create clusters of d12 hexes of the same terrain type.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSome Hexes have a @UUID[Compendium.celestus.rules.CapdrFIR5fQTiMqQ]{Barrier} on one or more of their edges, typically a sudden altitude change or impassible feature. These cannot normally be travelled through. For a typical Realm, place a number of Barriers equal to one sixth of your total Hexes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMost Realms have a navigable river passing through and a few large lakes spanning whole or multiple Hexes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 14\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"b7M2GiRfch140yQx","name":"Worthiness","pages":[{"_id":"Ht2bfnjbeskKAMS7","name":"Worthiness","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003eRank alone does not immediately grant the Knight a Council position or rule of a Holding. It merely proves their worthiness.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eA Knight may find themselves in a position for which their rank is unworthy. They are sure to face initial opposition, but if this can be overcome then their worthiness is proven.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eCore Rulebook, page 6\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}